 ## Background
-XPBD was introduced as an extension of Position-Based Dynamics (PBD) to address the limitations of hard constraints in PBD, such as instability and lack of tunable stiffness. It was notably used in the "Gaussian Splashing" framework for unified particle motion synthesis and rendering [S1]. The method converts the variational optimization problem of minimizing system potential energy into a series of constraint projections, making it computationally efficient and suitable for real-time applications [S1].
